        "committer": {
          "name": "Chell Laszlo",
          "email": "pumpkinbiscuit@proton.me",
          "date": "2026-11-12 02:05:25.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21132 build: take const mnt_idmap in VFS callbacks",
        "message": "LU-21132 build: take const mnt_idmap in VFS callbacks\n\nLinux commit v7.3-rc1-23-gc3150ded7bc0 (\"fs: port ->getattr() to pass\nconst mnt_idmap\") and the rest of the vfs-7.4-rc1.idmap series made\nthe idmap argument of the inode_operations and xattr_handler callbacks\nconst, so Lustre's callbacks no longer match the slot types.\n\nDeclare the callbacks with const struct mnt_idmap *idmap, as that\nkernel does.  For older kernels add a configure check and, next to the\nmacros that drop the argument for kernels without one, macros that\nstrip the const through ll_idmap_arg().  It works by token pasting, so\nthe argument must be named idmap in every callback.\n\nAlso define ll_get_acl() once per kernel variant, and rename the memfs\ndo_mkdir() to memfs_do_mkdir() so its macro does not clash with\nllite's do_mkdir().\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Chell Laszlo <pumpkinbiscuit@proton.me>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-fable-5-1\nChange-Id: Id31210f220c6f4369ceb87e2c357195d13e95714\n\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
